From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:16:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(telemetry): stamp session metadata on harness turn spans

Exported spans carry session.id but nothing about the session, so a
downstream job that classifies conversations has to look each session up
in the Omnigent database.

When OMNIGENT_TELEMETRY_ENABLED is on, the runner resolves session-level
attributes for every turn and forwards them on the turn body as
telemetry_attributes. The executor adapter binds them for the turn, and a
span processor stamps them on every span the harness emits.

- Read from the server each turn, so renames, label edits and project
  moves reach later spans: omnigent.session.title,
  omnigent.session.labels.<key> (internal omnigent.* labels skipped),
  omnigent.project.id and .name (the name is cached per project id),
  omnigent.agent.name, and omnigent.git.branch (the workspace's
  checked-out branch when the session records none).
- Resolved once per session on the runner: omnigent.workspace,
  omnigent.git.remote (credentials stripped), omnigent.host.name.

Every lookup is best-effort and bounded: the server reads share a short
budget, and a failure or timeout leaves the turn with the machine-local
attributes only; a turn is never delayed or failed by telemetry. The
session title is often generated from the first message, so it is
stamped only when OMNIGENT_OTEL_CAPTURE_CONTENT is on. Labels, project
and workspace are exported as metadata and documented as such.

No change when telemetry is disabled. There is no user attribute here.

Related: #10794

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
